    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup strategy today pivots heavily on leveraging favorable matchups against suspect pitching staffs, with **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.27) emerging as our strongest plays. Both benefit from high-leverage spots in the order and positive park factors, with **Dylan Beavers** specifically capitalizing on a +16% park boost against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez. **Bryce Harper** (68.70) remains an essential anchor in the 3-hole, bolstered by a +6% order bonus and strong xwOBA indicators, ensuring our offense maintains a high floor even against a competent starter in Warren. Conversely, **Cal Raleigh** (43.30) faces the steepest climb today; drawing deGrom is a high-risk scenario that severely dampens his scoring potential due to the elite skill profile of the opposing arm, making him a candidate to watch closely as the game develops.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Daulton Varsho** (43.90), who barely missed the starting cut. While his ability to exploit slow SP delivery offers potential for stolen bases\u2014a critical priority for our roster\u2014the negative pressure from a tough matchup against Suarez and unfavorable wind conditions pushed him below our efficiency floor for this slate. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (53.36) remains in the lineup despite a sub-standard efficiency score caused by a difficult matchup against Rasmussen, as his inherent base talent outweighs the potential for a swap. We are also monitoring **Gleyber Torres** (57.45); while his park factor is advantageous, his heavy platoon penalty against right-handed pitching requires cautious management as we balance our daily efficiency goals with the need to protect our remaining game caps for the stretch run.",
